  "title": "First the profit you want, then the price",
  "sourceHash": "sha256:7ee15b44079e5c4cc764e82d086cc72e281798936d6edacde8888b9c3288c90a",
  "outline": [
    {
      "heading": "The reverse order",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "The honest order is this: first the profit you want from the retreat, then all the costs, and only then the price.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "How many hours are in one retreat",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Paying yourself is a separate line, not whatever \"is left over\".",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "The lines people forget",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Besides the venue, the leader has their own costs.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "The price from the profit",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Prices are prices.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
